# Files that live in this repo but must NOT be served from
# guide.visitbahiapalace.com.
#
# This is a zero-config static deployment: by default Vercel publishes every
# file in the repo root, at its own URL. That included the two files below.
#
#   guide_content.json  — the COMPLETE narration script, all 17 stops in all
#                         five languages. It is the product. Nothing in the
#                         page ever fetched it (index.html renders short
#                         teasers from its own STOPS array), so it was 62KB
#                         of paid content sitting at a guessable URL, free,
#                         behind no gate at all.
#
#   generate_audio_edge_tts.py — the authoring tool. No secrets in it, but it
#                         is not part of the product and there is no reason
#                         to publish it.
#
# Both stay in git — guide_content.json is the master copy the audio is
# generated from, and the script needs it in the same folder to run. They
# are simply excluded from what gets uploaded.
#
# VERIFY AFTER DEPLOY. This file is the only thing standing between the
# script and the open internet, so confirm it actually worked:
#
#   curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" https://guide.visitbahiapalace.com/guide_content.json
#
# Expect 404. Anything else means the exclusion did not take effect.

guide_content.json
generate_audio_edge_tts.py
